/T (Conventional fine-tuning of massive models is prohibitively expensive; for example, fine-tuning a LLaMA 65B model can require your GPU memory to exceed 780 GB. By using PEFT methods like LoRA, you can bypass these extreme costs and fine-tune models on standard hardware, such as a Tesla T4 GPU, which operates within a much more accessible 2.06 GB VRAM footprint.)
